WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.901
[tense music]

00:00:01.968 --> 00:00:03.803
GORDON RAMSAY: I'm
30 feet down using

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:07.407
a diving system I've never
tried before called snuba.

00:00:07.474 --> 00:00:10.009
I'm trying to keep my air
hose from strangling me,

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:12.479
praying I don't run
into a great white.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:19.919
Below the surface, I try to
focus on finding a crayfish.

00:00:19.986 --> 00:00:21.755
I fight through the thick kelp.

00:00:21.821 --> 00:00:24.958
Underneath it, these
crays are hiding somewhere

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:26.159
in the nooks and crannies.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:33.066
Limbs on the line, I plunge
my hand into the unknown

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.969
of each dark hole.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:38.571
Damn, these crays
move like lightning.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:41.775
Finally, I manage to spot
a cray poking his head out

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:43.476
of a crack in the rock.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.378
It fights me with
all of its might,

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:48.715
using its powerful tail
to break from my grasp.

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:51.151
While I've done a little
diving in my life,

00:00:51.217 --> 00:00:52.752
I've never quite
experienced anything

00:00:52.819 --> 00:00:58.792
as majestic or rewarding
as catching a Tassie cray.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.594
[upbeat music]

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:05.932
Woo-hoo-hoo!

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.600
Oh my god.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:08.601
Yes!

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:09.569
Great job.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:10.270
Thank you.

00:01:10.336 --> 00:01:12.005
Seriously, well done.

00:01:12.071 --> 00:01:14.808
Look at the size of that, baby!

00:01:14.874 --> 00:01:17.110
That is a beauty.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:18.211
Man, they move fast.

00:01:18.278 --> 00:01:19.078
SHANE: Oh, yeah.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.113
Right.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:21.648
I can't wait to taste it, mate.

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:23.183
SHANE: Mate, they are the
sweetest thing you ever taste,

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.418
guaranteed.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.820
GORDON RAMSAY: Hard work done.

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.956
It's time for Shane to make
the most of this beauty

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:32.058
by cooking it two ways.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.260
While the amazing tail
goes into the pot,

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:37.597
Shane serves up some
crayfish sashimi.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:38.298
Look at it.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.733
A bit of soy in there.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.868
Bit of wasabi.

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:42.902
GORDON RAMSAY: Nice.

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.204
Look at that.

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.939
The sheen on that is
incredible, isn't it?

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.274
SHANE: Yeah.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:49.909
Bloody hell.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:51.578
That is [bleep] delicious.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:53.513
Always tastes a bit better
when you've earned it.

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:55.982
GORDON RAMSAY: Next, Shane
serves it simply steamed.

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:56.883
The money.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.284
This is where it's at.

00:01:58.351 --> 00:02:00.220
GORDON RAMSAY: Mate.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.588
Look at that, baby.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:02.956
Oh my lord.

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.290
Look at the weight of that.

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:06.059
I mean, it's enough for
six there, isn't there?

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.293
You've done
extremely well today.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.394
GORDON RAMSAY: Look at that.

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:12.732
Wow.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:14.234
That is delicious.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.835
Do you know what, I'm amazed
at the yield in terms of--

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.036
That's the muscle there.

00:02:17.103 --> 00:02:18.304
You felt the power
of how much it is,

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.607
and now you can see
how it all equates.

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:23.510
GORDON RAMSAY: That crayfish
was translucent, delicious,

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.846
meaty, sweet, and super firm.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.147
Incredible.

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:29.048
I'm definitely going
to use it to my feast

00:02:29.115 --> 00:02:30.183
at the end of the week.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.017
I'd love you to
come and join us.

00:02:31.084 --> 00:02:32.285
I would love to.

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.119
You know what goes
really well with this?

00:02:33.186 --> 00:02:34.654
A bit of wallaby.

00:02:34.721 --> 00:02:36.189
I think you need a bit of
game in there, a bit of meat.

00:02:36.256 --> 00:02:37.156
I know a lady that might
be able to help you out.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:38.391
Serious?
SHANE: Yeah.

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.626
Just ask any of the
locals for Sarah.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:40.793
Sarah.
SHANE: Yep.

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.161
Loves a bit of fire.

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:43.730
Yep, she'll be
right up your alley.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.732
The addition of a protein,
the wallaby, would be amazing.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:46.766
SHANE: Yeah.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.334
That's Tasmanian surf and turf.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:51.771
That has to be a
centerpiece of my feast.

00:02:51.838 --> 00:02:53.373
Do I do it like a surf and turf?

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:54.340
Do I keep it separate?

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:55.608
I got to think about that.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.044
But what I have got
is an amazing start,

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:01.748
because that crayfish is like
the Rolls Royce of the sea.

00:03:01.814 --> 00:03:02.916
Best for your travels.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:05.218
Can't wait to catch
you at the end.

